    description: "Penpot's official MCP server gives an LLM read and write access to a live Penpot design file — not just data queries but transformation and creation of design elements, which is what separates it from the read-only design connectors. The architecture is unusual and worth understanding before installing: the MCP server does not talk to a REST API, it talks to a dedicated Penpot MCP Plugin over a WebSocket, and the plugin executes code against Penpot's Plugin API inside the browser session. That means the assistant can write and run arbitrary Plugin-API snippets in the context of an open file, enabling design-to-design, code-to-design and design-to-code workflows. Setup has three moving parts: run the MCP server, run the web server that serves the plugin, and open the plugin inside Penpot so it connects. The server listens on port 4401 and exposes a Streamable HTTP endpoint at http://localhost:4401/mcp plus a legacy SSE endpoint at /sse; Claude Code adds it with `claude mcp add penpot -t http http://localhost:4401/mcp`, and stdio-only clients such as Claude Desktop bridge through `npx -y mcp-remote http://localhost:4401/sse --allow-http`. Requires Node.js (tested on v22.x). VERSION PINNING MATTERS HERE: the MCP server tracks the Penpot release it talks to, so run the tag that matches your instance — `npx -y @penpot/mcp@latest` for the current release on design.penpot.app, or a matching version for a self-hosted deployment. WHERE THE CODE LIVES: the server ships inside the main Penpot monorepo at github.com/penpot/penpot under `mcp/` (a pnpm workspace, driven by corepack — not a plain `npm install`). The older standalone `penpot/penpot-mcp` repo has not been updated since March 2026 and is not the version `@penpot/mcp` publishes from; build from the monorepo's `mcp/` directory if you want a source install. Star count shown is the Penpot platform repository's, since the MCP server is part of it. INSTALL COLLISION: the PyPI package `penpot-mcp` is NOT this server; it is Montevive's separate community Python server (montevive/penpot-mcp), so `pip install penpot-mcp` gives you different software with a different tool surface.",
    author: 'penpot',
    github_url: 'https://github.com/penpot/penpot',
    source_verified: true,
    verification: 'live',
    website_url: 'https://penpot.app',
    categories: ['media'],
    integrations: ['claude-desktop', 'cursor', 'cline'],
    install_type: 'npm',
    install_command: 'npx -y @penpot/mcp@latest',
    install_verified: true,
    install_checked: '2026-08-07',
    official: true,
    stars: 58394,
    featured: false,
