    slug: 'easypost-mcp',
    name: 'EasyPost MCP',
    description: 'EasyPost shipping API as an MCP server — get multi-carrier shipping rate quotes (USPS, UPS, FedEx and more) and track packages by tracking number, returning price, service level, estimated delivery days, and recent scan events as structured JSON. It runs as a hosted, remote server operated by Pipeworx rather than a local install: point your MCP client at `https://gateway.pipeworx.io/easypost/mcp` (or bridge it into a stdio-only client with `npx mcp-remote https://gateway.pipeworx.io/easypost/mcp`), and pass your EasyPost API key per-call as the `_apiKey` argument. Two tools are exposed — `easypost_rates` (from/to ZIP plus parcel weight → carrier rate options) and `easypost_track` (tracking code plus carrier → live status). It is one connector within the broader Pipeworx gateway, which fronts 1,300+ data sources behind a single MCP endpoint. Note: the npm package named `easypost-mcp` is an unrelated placeholder (its repository field resolves to a `your-org/…` template) and is not this server.',
