    slug: 'openstreetmap-mcp',
    name: 'OpenStreetMap MCP Server',
    description: 'jagan-shanmugam/open-streetmap-mcp (MIT, Python, 215+ stars) is the most-adopted OpenStreetMap MCP server, giving an assistant location-based tools built on the free OSM and Overpass APIs with no API key required. It covers geocoding an address to coordinates and the reverse, finding nearby points of interest by category and radius, retrieving details for a specific place, computing routes and travel distances between points, and running neighbourhood-style analysis — the "how walkable is this address, what is within ten minutes" class of question — plus schedule-aware queries that account for opening hours. It installs from PyPI as `osm-mcp-server` (note the package name differs from the repo name) and runs over stdio, so it drops into Claude Desktop, Cursor, or any stdio client with a one-line command entry. One thing to weigh before adopting: the repository was last pushed in July 2025, so it is stable rather than actively developed. If you need something under current maintenance, NERVsystems/osmmcp (Go, 28 stars, pushed March 2026) covers similar geospatial ground, and wiseman/osm-mcp (86 stars) is a third option — but neither has this one\'s adoption. All three query the same public OSM infrastructure, so please respect the Overpass API\'s fair-use limits when running bulk queries from an agent loop.',
