    description: 'Running a full MCP server on the ESP32 itself is not something any established project does today, and the searches that land here usually mean one of two other things. The first is embedded development assistance — letting an assistant drive the debugger and inspect a running target — which Adancurusul/embedded-debugger-mcp (Rust, ~138 stars) does over probe-rs or OpenOCD for ARM Cortex-M, RISC-V, and ESP32 parts; that is the mature option in this space and it runs on your workstation, not the microcontroller. The second is the Chinese-language XiaoZhi ESP32 voice-assistant ecosystem, where the device is an MCP *client* talking to a backend that holds the tools: joey-zhou/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java (~1,300 stars) and hackers365/xiaozhi-esp32-server-golang (~390 stars) are the substantial server implementations there, and the latter explicitly supports remote MCP tool invocation. Espressif\'s ESP-IDF is the official development framework for its chips and is where firmware work starts, but it is a toolchain and SDK — not an MCP server, and listing it as one confuses the two. This entry records no github_url until a genuine on-device ESP32 MCP server exists.',
