    slug: 'monetate-mcp',
    name: 'Monetate (No MCP Server Available)',
    description: 'Monetate is an enterprise experience-optimization platform for e-commerce, covering A/B and multivariate testing, audience building, content personalization, and AI-driven product recommendations (it absorbed the Certona recommendations engine along the way). Its corporate history is unusually tangled, which matters here: Kibo Commerce acquired Monetate, then later spun the personalization business back out under the Monetate brand in a sale to Centre Lane Partners, so Monetate is once again a standalone vendor rather than a Kibo product line. As of this review Monetate does not publish an MCP server, and no credible community project has built one either. This was checked four ways rather than by GitHub search alone: the GitHub Search API returns zero MCP-shaped repositories for Monetate; the monetate GitHub organization is real and holds 57 public repositories but an org-scoped search for mcp returns zero; the npm registry has no monetate-mcp, @monetate/mcp, or @monetate/mcp-server package; and a search of Monetate’s own site and documentation surfaces no MCP or agent-connector announcement. Do not confuse this with the Kibo Commerce MCP Server, which is real and hosted on each Kibo tenant — that belongs to Monetate’s former parent and covers catalog, orders, and inventory, not Monetate personalization. Until Monetate ships something, the practical route is wrapping the Monetate REST and recommendations APIs in your own small MCP server, or driving experiments through a listed experimentation server such as Optimizely, VWO, AB Tasty, or Kameleoon. This entry is kept so the term stays discoverable and will be replaced the moment a real server appears.',
