    description: 'wp-devdocs-mcp is a local MCP server that gives an AI coding assistant a verified WordPress hook database to query instead of recalling hook names from training data. It parses the actual source of WordPress core, WooCommerce, Gutenberg, or any plugin you point it at — including private and proprietary ones no model has ever seen — and builds a searchable index of every PHP action and filter (do_action, apply_filters, and their _ref_array variants), every JS hook (addAction, addFilter, applyFilters, doAction), every block registration (registerBlockType, registerBlockVariation), and JS API usage across wp.blocks, wp.blockEditor and wp.data. Since v1.1.0 it also parses handbook markdown into searchable pages. For each hook the assistant gets the exact name with dynamic-name detection for patterns like woocommerce_thankyou_{$payment_method}, the parameter list and count, file path and line number, the enclosing function and class, the docblock, and a code window of eight lines before and four after. The problem it solves is specific: models invent plausible hooks such as woocommerce_email_after_order_details that do not exist, reach for deprecated namespaces like wp.editor.InspectorControls instead of wp.blockEditor.InspectorControls, and miss newer HPOS-era hooks entirely. In an agentic loop that writes and tests its own code, one hallucinated hook name sends the agent debugging something that was never going to work.',
